Convert natural language descriptions into a JSON node graph.

## Available Node Types

### component (UI)
subtypes: button, input, text, card, container, list, image
props examples:
  button:    { label, variant: primary|secondary|ghost, disabled }
  input:     { placeholder, type: text|number|email }
  text:      { content, tag: p|h1|h2|h3|span, color }
  card:      { title, content, variant: default|glass|elevated }
  container: { direction: column|row, gap, padding }

### data
subtypes: state, props, number, string, array, boolean
props examples:
  state:  { name, value, dataType: number|string|boolean }
  number: { name, value }
  string: { name, value }
  array:  { name, value: [] }

### logic
subtypes: if, function, map, filter, reduce
props examples:
  if:       { condition }
  function: { name, params: "arg1,arg2", body }
  map:      { itemName, expression }
  filter:   { itemName, condition }

## Output Format (strict JSON)
{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "type": "component|data|logic",
      "subtype": "<subtype>",
      "label": "<Korean label>",
      "icon": "<emoji>",
